    shortTitle: "Word mark vs. logo",
    description: "Compare standard-character word marks with special-form logo applications and learn how the drawing affects the mark represented in a USPTO filing.",
    summary: "A standard-character drawing protects wording without claiming a particular font, style, size, or color. A special-form drawing protects the specific stylized wording, design, or color features shown. The choice affects the application record and the specimen needed to support it.",
